blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1859:	Each placement is a permutation of coordinates applied to a heterogeneous tensor product of the two block operators, so the multiplicative, adjoint and unit identities reduce to the corresponding identities for tensor products, and conjugation splits accordingly.  The two comparisons between player placements and block placements are proved entrywise, after inserting the identity on the registers that the coarser placement leaves untouched.  The one-sided conjugation identity follows from the split form of conjugation, because conjugating the identity by an operator with $UU^\dagger = \Id$ returns the identity on the other block.  The last three statements follow from the intertwining identity of Lemma~\ref{lem:extraction-register-transport-support} together with the existing norm statement for matrices satisfying $U^\dagger U = \Id$.
