  1668		identification of the game $\mathfrak{G}^{\mathrm{ld}}_{(q,m,d,1)}$ with
  1669		the two-prover tensor-code test for $\code^{\ot m}$, and neither that game
  1670		correspondence nor the bound on the auxiliary parameter of Theorem~4.7 under
  1671		which the stated error function $\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}$ is obtained has been
  1672		established. Both, with the divisibility obstruction, are documented in
  1673		\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}. Furthermore, the combined-lines
  1674		consistency of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-13}, on which
  1675		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-4-7} relies, is established here only with the error
  1676		$m \cdot \poly(\eps, md/q)$, the error form $\poly(m^2 \eps, md/q)$
  1677		carried in its statement remaining unproved; the discrepancy and the
  1678		established form are documented in
  1679		\cite{gap:qpbt_combined-lines-error-term}. The present proof is therefore
  1680		complete only modulo these four obligations. Since the
  1681		expanded state $\ket{\hat\psi}$ of Definition~\ref{def:expanded-state} is
  1682		exactly $\ket{\psi}$ with the halves of $M$ pairs
  1683		$\ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}$ appended locally in registers
  1684		$\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, we have
  1685		$\phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi}
  1686		= V_{\mathrm{A}} \ot V_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\hat\psi}$.
  1687		Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} therefore yields a state $\ket{\mathrm{aux}}$
  1688		on registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$ such that
  1689		\[
  1690			\bigl\| \phi_{\mathrm{A}} \ot \phi_{\mathrm{B}} \ket{\psi} - \ket{\mathrm{aux}} \ot \ket{\mathrm{EPR}_q}^{\ot M} \bigr\|^2 \leq \delta_{\mathrm{qld}}\;.
